WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.210
While Fire &amp; Blood states that Rhaenyra suffers
in childbirth for days, the show depicts her

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:06.990
labor as lasting one night.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:12.630
Her daughter, who she names Visenya, is stillborn
in both the book and the series, but Fire

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:16.369
&amp; Blood describes the child not only as deformed,
but part dragon.

00:00:16.369 --> 00:00:20.560
It's up to the reader's interpretation if
this means Rhaenyra's child was literally

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.240
a dragon-human hybrid, or if it's a euphemism
for the result of generations of incest.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:30.269
As we've seen in just one season of House
of the Dragon, Targaryen pregnancies don't

00:00:30.269 --> 00:00:31.810
have a great track record.

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:36.394
The fact that Rhaenyra managed to birth five
healthy children is practically a miracle.

00:00:36.394 --> 00:00:41.040
The House of the Dragon Season 1 finale doesn't
shrink away from her graphic sixth labor,

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.450
and lifeless Visenya is shown with a poorly
formed skull and missing limbs.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:50.180
Perhaps as a nod to her dragon-like qualities
in the book, Visenya's birth is intercut with

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:54.110
flashes of Syrax roaring as her rider wails
in pain and grief.

